{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.72,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U7", "H9", "P9"],
      "pins": ["U7.26", "U7.27", "H9.3", "H9.4", "P9.3", "P9.4"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "U7.26/H9.3", "U7.27/H9.4"],
      "observed": "In the 'Nutrition Pump B' block of the PERISTALTIC PUMP DRIVERS sheet, the Nutrient-B motor connector H9/P9 pins 3 and 4 — which on the identical Pump A and pH blocks carry the B-coil outputs from U7 pins 26/27 (OB1/BRB) — are additionally driven by two '+3V3' supply arrows, tying the +3V3 rail directly onto the B-phase coil lines (and thus shorting the two TMC2209 B outputs together through the supply).",
      "expected": "Per the spec, each TMC2209 'drives a 2-phase coil output (/A_xx+/-, /B_xx+/-) to connectors H7/H8/H9'; the coil lines must connect only between the driver outputs and the pump connector, with no connection to the +3V3 logic rail, exactly as drawn for U5/H7 and U6/H8.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 'PERISTALTIC PUMP DRIVERS', 'Nutrition Pump B': '+3V3' arrows tap the wires into H9 (JST_XH) / P9 (XH_2.5mm) pins 3 and 4, the same pins that receive U7 pin 26 (OB1) and pin 27 (BRB); the Pump A block (H8/P8) and pH block (H7/P7) show no such +3V3 connection on the corresponding coil pins."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Netlist: each drives a 2-phase coil output (/A_xx+/-, /B_xx+/-) to connectors H7/H8/H9, with its own current-sense resistor pair (R30–R35, 110 mΩ)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The Nutrient-B peristaltic pump's B coil is shorted to the +3V3 logic rail and the two B-phase driver outputs are bridged together through it. When U7 energizes the B phase, the TMC2209 output stage fights the 3.3 V LDO (U2) and the other coil line: the pump cannot dose, the +3V3 rail is loaded/contended, and U7 or U2 could be damaged. The other two dosing pumps are unaffected.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power tree, isolator channels, float interlocks and driver networks match the specification, but the Nutrition Pump B motor connector (H9/P9, B-coil pins 3/4) is shorted to the +3V3 rail — a deviation not present on the identical Pump A and pH blocks — so the design contains one anomaly."
}

